<!-- The NMIB adversary complaint's Word styles: the cross-engine recipe (tools/fb/src/docxxengine.rs) in the face of
     the typst template ({font}, Times New Roman) at 12 pt (LR 5.2(a): a serif font of 12 point or larger; size 24
     half points); Body Text in exact 24 pt line boxes (typst pitch: the numbered lines, double spacing) with a
     half-inch first-line indent, the headings in them with no space above or below (one numbered line each); the
     counsel block, caption and signature in 12 pt boxes (typst pitch-single, two lines per numbered line).
     docx/nmib-adversary-complaint.lua writes every paragraph's own spacing, the page (letter; margins 1.5 in top and
     bottom, 1.3 in left, 1 in right; the pleading rules as page borders) and the footer: the numbers 1 to 24 in a
     frame at the left of the numbered lines, and under the last one the page number, the paper's title and the case
     number (FORMBOOK_FOOTERS, FORMBOOK_FINAL). Twips: 20 x pt. -->
<reference xmlns:w="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/wordprocessingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" base="xengine" size="24" body="480" single="240" indent="720" heading="480" heading-before="0" heading-after="0"/>
